     "claim": "B_shutdown",
     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "On 19 April 2013 Gov. Deval Patrick asked more than a million greater Boston residents to shelter in place (a voluntary order; NBC/CBS: close to 1 million), mass transit was suspended, and the order was lifted at about 6 p.m. after the search of the Watertown neighbourhood was 'not fruitful'. The Globe itself calls it the 'decision to shut down Boston for manhunt'.",
     "urls": [
      "https://www.bostonglobe.com/metro/2014/04/19/patrick-reflects-decision-shut-down-boston-for-manhunt/HXbsrtnzSKxRDTIyMFWrMM/amp.html",
      "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/amp/wbna51619643",
      "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/boston-marathon-bombings-update-dzhokhar-tsarnaev-second-bombing-suspect-captured-alive-in-backyard-boat/",
      "https://www.npr.org/sections/thetwo-way/2013/04/19/177885868/shots-explosions-heard-as-boston-manhunt-continues"
     ]
    },
    {
     "claim": "B_found",
     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "After the order was lifted, a Watertown homeowner (David Henneberry; not named on screen) noticed something amiss with the boat in his backyard, went out to check it, found the cover's strap looser than usual, lifted the wrap, saw blood inside and called 911. The drawn boat is generic, with no name, number or make.",
     "urls": [
      "https://edition.cnn.com/2013/04/23/us/boston-attacks-boat-owner",
      "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/amp/ncna324991",
      "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/boston-marathon-bombings-update-dzhokhar-tsarnaev-second-bombing-suspect-captured-alive-in-backyard-boat/",
      "https://www.nbcboston.com/news/local/man-who-found-boston-marathon-bomber-in-his-boat-passes-away/29091/"
     ]
    }
